  "transcription": [
    "Transcribed by hand from the page images of the scan at 300 and 600 dpi. The PDF text layer is unusable and was not used. Every printed digit is kept.",
    "The tables print a mantissa and a power of ten (\"2.2699 + 2\"), with the power only on the first row of each block of ten rows and on the row where it changes. The `printed` strings use E notation with the power that applies to the row (\"2.2699E+2\").",
    "`printed` keeps the printed unit: pressure is in millibars. `si` is the printed value in SI (1 mb = 100 Pa exactly, Table 1 on page 2), with no other change. One count is one unit in the last printed digit (for \"2.2699E+2\" mb, 0.0001E+2 mb = 1 Pa).",
    "Page 57, Z = 8000 m: the second digit of P, \"3.5651\", is a damaged glyph read as 5 (the same row prints 2.6740E+2 torr, 356.50 mb). Page 65, Z = 47000 m: the row is smudged but every digit is legible.",
    "Page 67, Z = 84000 m: rho is printed 9.6940E-6 (confirmed at 600 dpi), 1.3 counts above eqs. 33a and 42 evaluated from the constants (9.69387E-6); the same row prints rho/rho0 = 7.9134E-6, which gives 9.6939E-6. It is transcribed as printed. Every other value is within one count of that evaluation (validation/oracles/ussa76/tables.py)."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Page 9: the ratio M/M0 of Table 8 was not included in the program that computed the tables below 86 km, so between 80 and 85.5 km the printed kinetic temperature T equals T_M, and the speed of sound and viscosities use that T. The page says tabulated T must be multiplied by M/M0 for the correct kinetic temperature and warns of a discontinuity of up to 0.04% between 85.5 and 86 km. Pressure and density do not depend on M/M0 below 86 km.",
    "At Z = 86000 m the table is computed from the upper-atmosphere model, so T = 186.87 K is the kinetic temperature (T_7 = 186.8673 K, eq. 25, page 10) and T_M = 186.95 K. From 86 km the table prints temperatures to 0.01 K and rho to 4 significant digits.",
    "Table III ends at Z = 85500 m (page 115; pages 18 and 19 say the speed of sound and the viscosities are tabulated only below 86 km), so the 86000 m row has null for those."
  ],
